> compile process. 

1) OO currently won't _run_ on FreeBSD Alpha - there is a specific piece
of code which needs to be written - FreeBSD Alpha gcc 2.95.2 bridge code 
in OO.
A few compaq engineers are busy working on Tru64 Alpha Compaq CC bridge
code, but even that one wasn't ready the last time I checked.
2) For painless usage, OO requires amount of RAM larger than that usually
found in old Alphas, so I wouldn't recommend it for Alphastations anyhow.

>
>
> hth,
>
> Jan
>

Regards,

Andrei


